<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55405" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατήκω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταταρτᾰρ-τάκω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱ]</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>melt</i> or <i>thaw away</i>, and in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be melted</i> or <i>thawed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δὲ χιὼν κατατήκετ᾽ . . ἥν τ᾽
					Εὖρος κατέτηξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.205
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὦπας δάκρυσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴν λύπαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					8.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατήκεσθαι τὸ θυμοειδές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.103
				</span></i>
			 K. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>dissolve</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίτρον κ. τὰς σάρκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.87
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				40.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii/iii A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέρα κ.
			πῦρ</span>, i.e. rarifies it, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				61a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὁ χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					221a31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ αἷμα</span>
			<i>dilute</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.262
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τέχνην εἴς τι</span>
			<i>waste</i> art and skill upon a thing, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				51
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, with pf.
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατέτηκα</span>, <i>melt away</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατήκομαι ἦτορ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.136
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σπλάγχνα κατατετηκότα ἐξάγειν</span>
			<i>dissolved</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.87
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατάκομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					187
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				977
			</span></i> (lyr., tm.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τοῖ . . ἄλγους κατατέτηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					1034
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρωτι κατατήκεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
				</span></i>
			
			
			<i><span class="en">
				8.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				104
			</span></i>: so with gen. added, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούτω κατετάκετο . . ἔρωτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					14.26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐν ψήφοις</span>
			<i>wear oneself away</i> in . . , <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
